<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hermanus van Wyk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1835">1835</a>–<a href="/years/1905">1905</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hermanus van Wyk was the first Kaptein of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rehoboth-namibia">Rehoboth</a> Basters in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a>. He led the Basters out of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> in 1868 and settled them at Rehoboth in 1870, and in 1885 he signed a protection treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> that preserved the community's autonomy. He led the community until his death in 1905.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hermanus-van-wyk.jpg" alt="Hermanus van Wyk" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hermanus_van_Wyk.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
